# Golden bytes: network NBT for a plain text component, as a real 26.1.2 server sends it.
#
# **Updated by acceptance (P10-11)**: the previous bytes were the compound form
# (0a 08 00 04 74 65 78 74 00 03 62 79 65 00), asserted as golden because the fixture and the
# encoder came from one reading. A real client joined, received our disguised_chat carrying
# that compound, and was kicked with a DecoderException -- the real-server capture (a console
# say) turned out to be a bare TAG_String, which the encoder now writes.
# What this body is: 6 bytes = TAG_String, empty root name, "bye".
08 00 03 62 79 65
